# Knobs for the Wayland session, sourced by /usr/local/bin/wayfire-session.
#
# This file exists so that a display problem on this vendor DRM stack can be
# bisected by editing one line and rebooting, instead of rebuilding and
# redeploying a 500 MB image for each attempt. Everything here is an
# environment variable wlroots or Mesa reads; the session script exports
# whatever this file sets.
#
# /etc is in the read-only squashfs, so an edit lands in the overlay -- which is
# exactly right for an experiment, and is wiped when the overlay is reseeded.
# A setting that turns out to be the answer belongs back in this file in the
# repository, with the reason written down.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Scanout buffer layout.
#
# ON, and not an experiment. The Mali renders into an ARM AFBC buffer
# (modifier 0x800000000000062: 32x8 blocks, SPLIT|SPARSE) and the AFBC decoder
# in aml_drm cannot read that layout back -- it produced "*ERROR* afbc error
# happened, 6-1" in bursts and a picture that came apart in bands. This forces
# the buffer the display reads to be linear. The GPU still renders with AFBC.
WLR_DRM_NO_MODIFIERS=1

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# On-screen keyboard languages.
#
# The keyboard key in wvkbd cycles this ordered list. English and Russian are
# enabled in the production image; symbols stay as the last page. The bundled
# mobintl keyboard can also load arabic, persian, greek, georgian, hebrew,
# emoji, nav and dialer. A user can override these two variables without root
# in ~/.config/chiron/keyboard.conf; wayfire-session reads that file after this
# one. The new list takes effect at the next login.
WVKBD_LAYERS=full,cyrillic,special
WVKBD_LANDSCAPE_LAYERS=landscape,cyrillic,landscapespecial
# Example user override adding Greek to both orientations:
# WVKBD_LAYERS=full,cyrillic,greek,special
# WVKBD_LANDSCAPE_LAYERS=landscape,cyrillic,greek,landscapespecial

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Direct scanout.
#
# OFF, and the reason is written here so the same idea is not tried twice.
#
# The symptom is a vertical video played fullscreen at transform 0 (the panel's
# native portrait): the picture comes apart into horizontal bands, each showing
# a different moment of the video. Rotate to transform 270 and it is clean. That
# looked like direct scanout -- at transform 0 a fullscreen client buffer can go
# straight to the display plane, while a rotated output must be composited and
# so never takes that path -- so this was set to 1 and tested.
#
#     WAYFIRE_DISABLE_DIRECT_SCANOUT=1
#
# It made no difference: the bands were unchanged, and a grim capture -- which
# reads what the compositor produced, not what the plane displayed -- showed the
# bands in the composited buffer. Whatever tears this frame has already torn
# before the display controller sees it, so the plane path is not the cause.
#
# Left off. Disabling it means compositing every fullscreen frame through the
# GPU, which on this board costs bandwidth that video playback needs.
